<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42924" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scēpsis</span></b> , is,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκῆψις,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in
			Mysia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 32, §
			122</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Scēp-sĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Scepsis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Metrodorus,</span>”
				<i>of Scepsis</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 1, 24, 59</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 7, 16, § 34</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also called simply Scepsius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 14, 38</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
